ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÁÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÁÄ
  LACK OF REGISTRATION REQUIREMENTS
ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

Registration is NOT required to run SRE.  SRE might be classified as one of
these types of programs:

Shareware - Yes!  SRE is shareware.  You are required to register this game
            after 99 years of trial use!
Freeware - Yes!  SRE could be considered freeware.  (However, freeware is
            a trademarked term.)  You are not required to pay any fee for
            this program.  However, we do give benefits to those who donate
            $15 or more.
Crippleware - Yes!  SRE is slightly crippled!  You can't access the bank in
            the unregistered version.  (But you don't need the bank to play
            the game.)
Bogusware - Yes!  SRE is bogusware!  It will destroy itself after 99 years!
            (If you don't register!)  (just kidding!)
Deadware - Yes!  You must've found the bugs!
Bonusware - Yes!  If you register, you get bonuses (like the bank)!

(I prefer to think of it as Bonusware.)

ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ
  REGISTRATION COST
ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

Seriously,

Registrationø is only $15 (U.S. dollars) for SRE 0.99x, so go ahead and
register!  All we want to know is some basic information, and if you like,
you can fill out the survey as well.  We may use survey results to determine
what operating systems, machines, and BBS software to support in future games.

*** To register, fill out Docs/SREReg.TXT and send it in.øø ***

What we do is send you a registration code that you type into SRE and it
will register itself.  We do not create a 'registered version' or send you
a disk.  The reason?  In many games, you can register one version and the
next version requires a new fee for upgrade.  For SRE, you get the numbers
that work in ALL versions of SRE.  That way, you will be able to get all
future versions for free from local BBSes.

NOTE: We do not register this game under handles (for various reasons).
      If you wish to see where your name will appear, run SRE SYSOP
      and choose "Registered Version".

Non-US persons:  Checks / money orders must be US funds from a U.S. bank.
                 Otherwise, send US cash or an international money order.
                 (in Canada, the Post Office can issue Money Orders in
                 U.S. funds.)

                 You may also wish to get together with other sysops in
                 your area to register together; you will save on the
                 currency conversion charges and also on postage.  I
                 will send the registrations to each person separately.

Make out checks or money orders to "Amit J. Patel".  Sorry, NO credit card
orders.  Expect 2-3 weeks to receive your numbers.  We try to handle
everything as fast as possible, but sometimes it just doesn't get done
soon enough.

Registration is not required in order to run this game, but we'd like
you to register this game!  The benefits of registering are:

  ş Automatic registration of all new versions.  (See above.)
  ş The Bank - loan, savings, and investments
  ş More Attack types - chemical, nuclear, and psionic
  ş Customization - you can set the number of turns, the number of
    planets available, the galactic tax rate, and the bank interest.

Please first evaluate this software and determine whether users on your BBS
enjoy it; it makes little sense to register a program without trying it out,
then later complaining that nobody likes it!

If you have any more questions, please send a letter to the address listed in
the registration form.

Thanks for registering!

--
ø By "Registration", I'm NOT trying to imply that you MUST register, like
  many other programs; this program IS free, but the "registration fee" is a
  donation to enable extra features in the game.  You are NOT required
  to register, like most shareware programs.

øø Registration takes several weeks (2 to 4); if you wish to avoid delays,
   please do the following:
        1 - Type the information into SREREG.TXT and then print it out
            instead of writing it by hand.
        2 - If you are registering more than one game, please print out
            separate registration forms and include separate checks.  Mehul
            and I are _not_ the same person!  If you send a form to him,
            and you write at the bottom "register SRE also", I will not
            read that form until 3 weeks after he gets it (he has to finish
            the registration first), and then it may be ANOTHER 3 weeks
            before I do registrations.
        3 - If you must write the information by hand, please write neatly!
            Many times, we have gotten mail back from the post office because
            we were unable to read the address and our interpretation wasn't
            the right one.
        4 - Use full-sized paper instead of small pieces; small slips of
            paper are more easily lost.
        5 - It does not help to send it through express mail; since it takes
            2 to 4 weeks, one or two days is not going to make a big
            difference.  Also, my experience with the postal service
            is that it usually takes 2 or 3 days for "snail" mail to
            arrive.

ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ
  SOURCE CODE TO SRE / DOOR PROGRAMMING KIT
ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

      It is our policy not to distribute any source code for our games.
      However, we do have complete source for the DOOR portion of the
      DOOR GAME.  (We just don't release the GAME portion.)  For SRE,
      we use SRCOMM version 2.  SRCOMM 2 has modem I/O, disk I/O, a
      Resource.Dat reader, an ANSI to screen interface (so that sysops
      don't need ANSI.SYS loaded), interfaces to SRDOOR, command line
      parameter handling, error logging, transcripts of user actions, a
      cooperative multitasker, and some other little things.  My next game
      uses SRCOMM version 3.  SRCOMM 3 has the features of SRCOMM 2, but it
      is much easier to get a game started, and includes a working demo
      game.  It also has Fossil driver support, better status bar
      customization, hot key support, SRE's menu routines, time slicing
      routines, a string class, an array class, and a better Resource.Dat
      reader that can read multiple values for each resource.

      My goal is to make door game writing very simple.  Output is very
      similar to C++'s streams, with additional support for colors, but
      without support for the advanced formatting and floating point
      number output.  Here's a bit of code from the demo game included
      in SRCOMM 3:

        kout << Tab(40) << "Hi there!!\n";
        kout << "Your sysop is " << GAME.sysop << "!\n";

      For most output, you can just search and replace cout with kout,
      and add some initialization code to start the SRCOMM library, and
      things will work.

      For Turbo Pascal, we have SRCOMMP, our communication routines from
      BRE.  Unlike the C++ routines, we don't include a lot of general
      purpose utility code (like file, array, and string classes) or a
      demo game.  However, the goal is the same -- SIMPLE game writing.
      You don't have to learn a new set of output routines; you can still
      use Write and Writeln along with all the formatting that comes with
      those commands.

      Instead of Writeln('Hi there!!'), you would use
                 Writeln(Com,'Hi there!!');
      We have written a virtual device driver called Com that can works
      for both screen and remote output, and uses direct or Fossil
      communication routines.

      Both the C++ and Turbo Pascal versions of our door kits come with
      full source, but unfortunately, neither comes with good
      documentation.  :-(  The C++ version is tested with Turbo C++ 3.0
      and Borland C++ 3.0, 3.1, and 4.0.  The C++ version will work with
      Borland C++ for OS/2 in the near future.

ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ
  I CAN'T AFFORD TO REGISTER!
ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

      If you do not have the money to register, you do not have to remove
      the game, like so many others.  You have 99 years as a "trial"
      period.  The only thing you will be missing is the ability to set the
      number of turns and set up the bank (and some other minor things).

ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ
  LIST OF GAMES
ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

      AC6 - Alpha Colony 6
            0.950 - latest release

            AC6 is similar to SRE in style & play.  It's written by a
            different programmer in a different language; it's not exactly
            the same; it takes many of the same types of actions and extends
            them (12 types of attack instead of 5, using multiple covert
            agents in a covert op, and stocks are just some examples).
            It is not well-supported, and it still has many bugs.

      PC  - Planetary Conquest
            2.0 - latest release
            PC is no longer supported.  Registrations are not accepted;
            all registered-only features are now available in the
            unregistered version.

            Planetary Conquest is a strategy game placed on a 20x20 on-screen
            board.  There are several playing pieces, each with a different
            purpose, strength, move, and weapon.  There are Soldiers, Tanks,
            Bases, Artillery, Walls, Obstacles/Symbols, and Water.  There are
            20 scenarios that can be played by 2 to 4 players.

      SCE - Solar Conquests Elite
            1.1 - latest release
            SCE is no longer supported.  Registrations are not accepted.

            Solar Conquests Elite is similar to PC, but is based in space.
            There are 5 types of ships and several weapon/engine types.
            The game allows from 2 to 5 players to play.

      LEA - Lost Empires of Arcadia
            0.990 - latest release
            LEA is not currently supported.  Registrations are not accepted.

            Lost Empires of Arcadia is a huge game with lots of races of
            beings, castles, thieves, wizards, assassins, many types of
            warfare, etc.  There are of course, many bugs!  :(  We do not
            have the full source due to hard disk errors, so it is very
            unlikely that we will be fixing the game.  :(

      SRH - Solar Realms Hangman
            0.990 - latest release

            This is a computer version of the popular 'Hangman' game.  You
            can enter words and other players have to guess them.  The winner
            gets to enter another word or phrase, and the process continues.

      BRE - Barren Realms Elite
            0.970 - latest releases change every day, so I don't have the
            right version number.

            This is a new game that is better than SRE, not only in play,
            but in allowing you to play against other BBSes through
            Fidonet.  There are more covert ops, more trading options, a
            trading market, better warfare, nicer news files, and best of
            all - Inter-BBS operations!  (Many people feel, that for
            single-BBS play, SRE is better than BRE, but BRE shines in
            its multiple-BBS capability.)

      SRE - Solar Realms Elite
            0.994   latest release version

            SRE is this game!  SRE is different from BRE in several (small)
            ways:  (1) fewer bugs; (2) Flavors; (3) an optional
            non-inflationary economic rule set; (4) research planets that
            let you improve the capabilities of your other planets and
            military.

